# Build output
build/
cmake-build-*/
*.pbw
.lock-waf_*

# Generated by tools/pnx_assets.py. Deliberately not committed: they are derived from
# the manifest and the source art, and committing them would let a stale blob outlive the
# manifest that describes it -- exactly the mismatch the blob version field exists to
# catch. Run the pipeline after cloning.
examples/*/resources/*.bin
examples/*/resources/preview_*.png
examples/*/src/c/assets_gen.h

# NOT ignored, and deliberately so: examples/*/maps/*.pnxmap. A `.pnxmap` is a map's
# SOURCE -- the thing an author edits -- and it is binary only because a character grid
# cannot hold the tile count. The compiled map_*.bin above IS derived and is ignored. A
# binary file in a repository invites the opposite assumption, which is why this says so.

# Editor and preview output
preview.html
tools/__pycache__/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Frozen editor binaries from tools/build_editor.py. Platform-specific and ~20MB each,
# so they belong on a release page rather than in the history.
dist/

# Local environments and IDE state
.venv/
venv/
.idea/
node_modules/

# Alloy scripting artefact from the probe lineage
src/c/mc.ffi.c

# Reference MIDI kept locally for analysis. Not committed: these are other people's
# compositions, and a public MIT repo is the wrong place for them. The importer is the
# deliverable; the songs it reads are the user's own business.
*.mid
*.midi
